{"extract": "Safiya Hussaini Tungar Tudu (born 1967) is a Nigerian woman condemned  to death for adultery in 2002. She gave birth to a child as a single woman in Sokoto, a Nigerian state under Sharia law. She was sentenced to be stoned, but was acquitted of all charges in March 2002 after a retrial.", "links": [{"ns": 1, "title": "Talk:Safiya Hussaini", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Capital punishment", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Nigerian", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Nigerians", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Retrial", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Sharia", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Sokoto (city)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Stoning", "exists": true}, {"ns": 4, "title": "Wikipedia:Basic copyediting", "exists": true}, {"ns": 4, "title": "Wikipedia:Manual of Style", "exists": true}, {"ns": 4, "title": "Wikipedia:Writing better articles", "exists": true}, {"ns": 12, "title": "Help:Maintenance template removal", "exists": true}]}